      "writtenOn": "2022-10-17T13:34:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is better than emitting invalid SPIR-V, for sure. \n\nHowever, for a long time we\u0027ve had a goal to avoid emitting errors from the backend as much as possible, and push errors up to the front. For Runtime Effects this was a big deal, because it was the difference between \"user gets a reasonable compile error\" and \"user compiles a shader with no error reports, but painting mysteriously does nothing.\"\n\nI\u0027m not sure if that goal applies here because Runtime Effects will never be able to directly specify a sampler2DRect. WDYT Brian?",
      "revId": "49ee8cc6b4c5753d9896fdc5b597895dc0d05661",
